CORE
main.c
--enforce-contract foo _ --enforce-contract bar _ --pointer-check
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^.*Only one contract may be enforced at a time.*$
^.*DFCC instrumentation has already been applied.*$
This test enforces contracts on two different functions across two
separate goto-instrument invocations on the same goto binary. This
case is intentionally allowed for the non-DFCC path: each function
gets its own __CPROVER_contracts_original_<F> wrapper, so the wrappers
do not conflict and the per-function guard does not fire. The final
cbmc run confirms the twice-enforced binary still verifies, i.e.
enforcing distinct functions across invocations yields a correct goto
binary -- equivalent to enforcing both in a single invocation.
